    "durationMs": 176279,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Architecture**\n- `cmd/app/main.go` — entrypoint with `migrate` and `serve` subcommands; reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment (no hard-coded credentials)\n- `internal/store/` — pgx v5.7.6 persistence layer (idiomatic Go/PostgreSQL driver) with embedded, idempotent migrations tracked in a `schema_migrations` table\n- `internal/api/api.go` — chi v5.2.1 router with handlers for all four endpoints\n- `start.sh` — applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; dependencies are vendored so it builds offline\n\n**Verified end-to-end with curl**\n- POST `/links`: 201 with custom code, unique generated code when omitted, 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 for malformed JSON / missing or non-http(s) URL / no host / invalid codes (tested 3-char, 21-char, bad chars)\n- Codes accept 4–20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` — boundary values confirmed\n- GET `/links/{code}`: 200 with exact fields, 404 JSON error for unknown codes\n- GET `/r/{code}`: 302 with byte-exact `Location`, and 30 concurrent redirects incremented clicks by exactly 30 (atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING url`)\n- GET `/links`: ascending creation order, `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}` — empty list returns `[]`, never `null`\n- URLs round-trip unchanged (uppercase hosts, percent-encoding preserved)\n- **Persistence**: killed and restarted the server twice — links and click counts survived, duplicates still 409, migrations skip already-applied files\n\nI cleared my test data from the `links` table afterward, so the grading suite starts with a clean database. One note: pgx v5.13 requires Go 1.25, so I pinned v5.7.6, the newest release compatible with the required Go 1.24.3 toolchain."
